tput on OS-9 -- what was changed===============================Badri Lokanathan's tput, comp.sources.unix volume 7, release 2 (1986).The original is in ORIG/ and is what everything below is measured against.Two changes, both under #ifdef OSK, so ORIG still builds elsewhere:1.  <sgtty.h> -> <sgstat.h> (tput.h).  OS-9 keeps terminal modes in    <sgstat.h>; the struct and the ioctl names differ, and only the    include was needed here.2.  The cursor-motion branch (tput.c) turned XTABS off around its output    and restored it afterwards, so that a tab inside a cursor-motion    string reached the terminal whole.  OS-9 holds that setting in the    path descriptor rather than in sg_flags, and SCF does not expand    tabs on output, so there is nothing to turn off: the string is    written as it stands.One thing that is NOT a change, and cost an hour before it was readproperly: l68 reported    Symbol 'errno' defined by psect 'tput_c' ... has already appeared    in psect 'cstart_a'Microware's cstart defines errno, so tput.h declares it (extern interrno) rather than defining it.  The accompanying message, "Symbol'main' ... caused name clashes", names the psect, not the culprit.Capability names are System V's, not termcap's -- that is the program,not the port.  `tput clear', not `tput cl'; `tput cup 10 20', not`tput cm'.  The table is in tput.h.  Release 1 used termcap names andthe author changed them deliberately: "Totally different capabilitynaming conventions from first release, but equivalent to SVconventions."